{
  "name": "Back to Back",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>When you're within 5 feet of a creature on your turn, you can expend one superiority die and optionally switch places with that creature, provided you spend at least 5 feet of movement, the creature is willing, and isn't Incapacitated. This movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.</p><p>Roll the superiority die. Until the start of your next turn, you or the other creature (your choice) gains a bonus to AC equal to the number rolled. This effect ends early if either of you become Incapacitated or you are more than 5 feet away from each other. The AC bonus from this maneuver does not stack with that from Evasive Footwork.</p>",
